    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#description -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#description">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/>
        <TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>RootEntity</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
        <TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>
        <rdf:label>description</rdf:label>
        <rdfs:comment>&quot;This is a string, and defines a textual free-form description of the object.

Notes:

This attribute doesn’t exist in M.3100. The CIM has two attributes for this purpose, Caption (a short description) and Description.&quot;</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#name -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#name">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#Attribute"/>
        <TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>RootEntity</TMF_SID_v1:hasOrigin>
        <TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_SID_v1:hasStereotype>
        <rdf:label>name</rdf:label>
        <rdfs:comment>Represents a user-friendly identifier of an object. It is a (possibly ambiguous) name by which the object is commonly known in some limited scope (such as an organization) and conforms to the naming conventions of the country or culture with which it is associated. It is NOT used as a naming attribute (i.e., to uniquely identify an instance of the object).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_SID_v1#status -->

